  message: "Done in PR #2337 (dev a037577a4), found while working WI-rasok and fixed more generally than the FIX asked: symbol_kind, framework_role and meta_match are now checked once, before any match type (Pattern._also_required), so they bind the parent_base_class / method_name arm AND the decorator, base_class and annotation arms (kafka-connect.yaml's four base_class + symbol_kind rows had the same hole).\n\nTHE FILED CASE, RE-RUN (fixture ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/rasok_11222026/fixtures/litfx: package.json with lit, a LitElement subclass with render() and updated(), and top-level functions render() and updated(); hypergumbo run, lit detected in both arms): at 8c2159eab the FUNCTIONS render and updated carry render_method / lifecycle_hook [lit]; at dev a89850612 they carry neither, and the methods MyElement.render and MyElement.updated keep theirs.\n\nTests: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_method_name_rows.py (TestKindRoleAndMetaBindEveryMatchType, and a scan of every shipped row for a pair of match-by fields the matcher does not conjoin). Mutation controls: dropping the kind check reds 7 tests, dropping the conjunct 9.\n\nNot measured: a real Lit repository (none on this machine; Tone.js/examples has two Lit files and shows no change)."  # b573
